{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/build.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:24:31.784391Z","id":"7a96ebb5ba932b732f23b33736801444b64544c02261b89bafd8ba593ec05bae","body":{"detail":"lane_worker in scripts/quality_gates.sh runs crates/clax-worker/test-wasm.mjs, which runs build.sh: off macOS it uses clang and the newest llvm-ar* on PATH, and on its first run cargo installs worker-build 0.8.7 into target/tools (minutes, cold). .github/workflows/ci.yml:13 and rust-toolchain.toml add the wasm32-unknown-unknown target. Whether ubuntu-latest's clang targets wasm32 and has an llvm-ar, and how long the lane takes cold there, was not checked; the first CI run shows it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":13},"end":{"line":19},"content_hash":"041427a2c0539298d3df3b7ce38d3930263f6d5702d96afa69c26ad1e5cf1d5b"},"summary":"The worker lane's wasm build has run only on macOS: CI's Ubuntu runner and build.sh's Linux branch are unverified","tags":["gates","ci","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/Cargo.toml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:17:08.819630Z","id":"93f1c8f7fcce808be359bfa4edee23928f3fbeab6bb9e2d764001a0b0f0b420a","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-worker is its own workspace and uses clax-core, clax-rt and clax-server by path; its Cargo.lock was extended from the spike's, not seeded from the root Cargo.lock. A dependency the root pins (axum 0.8.9, rusqlite 0.40.2 agree today) can drift. Joining the root workspace would share one lockfile but pull workers-rs into every native build.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":25},"end":{"line":31},"content_hash":"3009a302208a3d2a63dba6e2cdbc23240a6e50a624d65c65da64b7be7cfbf5eb"},"summary":"The Worker's lockfile resolves the Clax crates' dependencies apart from the root's, so the Worker may build them at other versions than the daemon","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/e2e-clone.mjs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T11:16:47.746409Z","id":"9490f5aaa9b490a578907887ffe222d66d8a93de6e5067baa854cdca51cb820c","body":{"detail":"On the Worker every browser is a LAN viewer (record df3fe77c on crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs, hosted: None), so no browser reaches the git token routes as a person. The check sends Authorization: Bearer <CLAX_TOKEN> with every request, frame content included, and with it the page shows 'Comment mode could not load in this page' (the bridge on the artifact origin); the Clone checks do not depend on it. Once the Worker serves signed-in members (hosted mode), the check should sign a member in instead.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":76},"end":{"line":80},"content_hash":"8e3a4b0a50d6a53ed34fdedc3586ea9aef33f7e961dc8c72915045e868eacb08"},"summary":"The Clone dialog's Worker check signs the browser in by sending the owner token on every request: the Worker has no owner browser yet","tags":["status:deferred","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/Cargo.toml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T11:27:26.058068Z","id":"af73cb2ed383f881021b778eb2194604afc102070e02a2aec2299aed7bb0c6b6","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-worker is its own workspace and uses clax-core, clax-rt and clax-server by path; its Cargo.lock was extended from the spike's, not seeded from the root Cargo.lock. A dependency the root pins (axum 0.8.9, rusqlite 0.40.2 agree today) can drift. Joining the root workspace would share one lockfile but pull workers-rs into every native build.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":25},"end":{"line":31},"content_hash":"b4c283574e347d9e3c895617432c5fd93a908f1f9277cc5f7cce8804ba4aca1d"},"summary":"The Worker's lockfile resolves the Clax crates' dependencies apart from the root's, so the Worker may build them at other versions than the daemon","supersedes":"93f1c8f7fcce808be359bfa4edee23928f3fbeab6bb9e2d764001a0b0f0b420a","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/e2e-clone.mjs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T11:58:17.360120Z","id":"21c1bcecc8c950072d2ce2c4ca94f3a4c2e8d5ab3a22e224e3e8220feb0e3a0f","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:5be6ea74","summary":"Fixed: the check runs the Worker hosted and signs Ada in with the setup secret, her browser carrying only its session cookie; npm run e2e:clone passes every check, including 'the page shows no comment-mode failure' at 1280 and 390, light and dark, and Sam offered read alone.","supersedes":"9490f5aaa9b490a578907887ffe222d66d8a93de6e5067baa854cdca51cb820c","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/e2e-publish.mjs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:13:10.748920Z","id":"e7e61e071d45155206aa092dc95df07d7f20eb8b84162af3b2867e2c9de80a56","body":{"detail":"Like e2e-hosted.mjs, it runs only by hand (npm run e2e:publish with CLAX_TEST_BIN set), since it needs a clax binary beside the Worker build. The native path is covered in the gates by crates/clax-server/tests/api_remotes.rs and crates/clax-cli/tests/remote_push.rs.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1},"end":{"line":12},"content_hash":"75d8bcda59fdd9cffe6a5608889f53cf63c50ffac07fc242b1547da2433a1784"},"summary":"The Worker's publish e2e is not run by scripts/quality_gates.sh","tags":["testing","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/deploy.mjs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:34:23.231877Z","id":"514d6135284b54f9bfaa4bcf914f69f84183228301ae0a447aeb5f3154b2d840","body":{"detail":"Only the logged-out --dry-run ran (no account was available): node deploy.mjs --dry-run --zone example.com passes and ends at wrangler deploy --dry-run (11.36 MiB, 4.36 MiB gzipped). Each logged-in step throws with wrangler's last error line and the command it ran, so a wrong pattern shows as a failed step rather than silently. If namespaces list answers a shape jsonIn does not parse, the namespace is taken as missing and a probe repository is created and deleted, which is harmless.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":160},"end":{"line":230},"content_hash":"3f94c1ef605bbf4f9236d3a3617324915d8794ac3882a04c08cb89544e148941"},"summary":"deploy.mjs's logged-in paths have not run: the whoami --json accounts shape, the 'already exists' patterns for r2 bucket create and queues create, artifacts namespaces list --json's shape, secret list --format json, and the account-scoped deploy with --secrets-file","tags":["deploy","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/deploy.mjs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:34:23.231915Z","id":"df81d2fea0c34dd89187eef2a82e7df5abfabd2356205a8e68bf76b73e7c0193","body":{"detail":"The owner is told to delete the record once set up; CLAX_TOKEN there stays valid until rotated (deploy.mjs --rotate-secrets). An alternative is printing them only and having smoke-remote.mjs take them from the environment, at the cost of the one-command smoke.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":276},"end":{"line":281},"content_hash":"414d576933fd9210f222e847e6f372f2975ebe1fa1583e8a77b8eedd6675d13d"},"summary":"deploy.mjs keeps the generated SETUP_SECRET and CLAX_TOKEN in plain text in crates/clax-worker/.deploy/<public host>.json (0600, git-ignored) so smoke-remote.mjs can use them","tags":["deploy","security","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/smoke-remote.mjs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:34:23.232163Z","id":"4854d787a4833aea89d19dd5e75c7a3143dfe78c2612be02169652b1731c3277","body":{"detail":"wrangler's docs say remote: true on an artifacts binding uses the remote service in local dev; whether that holds with --local and wrangler 4.149.0 is unverified. Locally the binding answers 'Binding ARTIFACTS needs to be run remotely'. If it works it gives a probe of the real service without a deploy.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":583},"end":{"line":588},"content_hash":"765d646f83c57f6bfd8c11ce9c56e0694989cbb0bd8310228dc0a9cf9e38cdfc"},"summary":"--remote-artifacts (the local Worker on the account's real Artifacts through the binding's remote: true) has not run: it needs a login, and harness.mjs starts wrangler dev with --local","tags":["deploy","artifacts","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/deploy.mjs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:04:35.038836Z","id":"1cdb4d61ee59652c4354b89553a4e030696e48a5382d37f7e827c80cdab0cfad","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"df81d2fea0c34dd89187eef2a82e7df5abfabd2356205a8e68bf76b73e7c0193","summary":"Checked: writeRecord writes the record with mode 0o600 and chmods it 0600 again, and crates/clax-worker/.gitignore lists .deploy/. Plain-text storage itself is unchanged; left open for the owner.","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/test-repos.mjs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:46:48.117278Z","id":"a3e8251c3f14d646150e8c2a8d326dd42aa53683c1de7647a870e7959b5737cc","body":{"detail":"Run in sequence after the other Worker e2e lanes; two later runs alone passed. The Worker answers the oversized body before reading it (the body caps), which wrangler dev's proxy sometimes turns into a lost connection. The e2e-hosted lane follows its chunked oversized bodies with a request that may fail for the same reason.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":584},"end":{"line":585},"content_hash":"df0793a0b2b4eb9b97ad52f463593d700501072fbce6616032fdcc9bf4fc1e85"},"summary":"The 13 MiB push check failed once in three runs: git saw HTTP 500 where 413 was expected, wrangler logging 'Network connection lost' for the receive-pack POST","tags":["worker","test","flake","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/deploy.mjs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:30:25.931134Z","id":"61c8252ad530041c277dd059809fb9481703393efcc1eced47a4d98523f42ed2","body":{"detail":"Only the logged-out --dry-run ran (no account was available): node deploy.mjs --dry-run --zone example.com passes and ends at wrangler deploy --dry-run (11.36 MiB, 4.36 MiB gzipped). Each logged-in step throws with wrangler's last error line and the command it ran, so a wrong pattern shows as a failed step rather than silently. If namespaces list answers a shape jsonIn does not parse, the namespace is taken as missing and a probe repository is created and deleted, which is harmless.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":164},"end":{"line":234},"content_hash":"3f94c1ef605bbf4f9236d3a3617324915d8794ac3882a04c08cb89544e148941"},"summary":"deploy.mjs's logged-in paths have not run: the whoami --json accounts shape, the 'already exists' patterns for r2 bucket create and queues create, artifacts namespaces list --json's shape, secret list --format json, and the account-scoped deploy with --secrets-file","supersedes":"514d6135284b54f9bfaa4bcf914f69f84183228301ae0a447aeb5f3154b2d840","tags":["deploy","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/deploy.mjs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:30:25.931134Z","id":"bef595b64d34d5bcbde5cd7bd6be41ded484d86fee253b6418123a0514d03583","body":{"detail":"The owner is told to delete the record once set up; CLAX_TOKEN there stays valid until rotated (deploy.mjs --rotate-secrets). An alternative is printing them only and having smoke-remote.mjs take them from the environment, at the cost of the one-command smoke.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":280},"end":{"line":285},"content_hash":"414d576933fd9210f222e847e6f372f2975ebe1fa1583e8a77b8eedd6675d13d"},"summary":"deploy.mjs keeps the generated SETUP_SECRET and CLAX_TOKEN in plain text in crates/clax-worker/.deploy/<public host>.json (0600, git-ignored) so smoke-remote.mjs can use them","supersedes":"df81d2fea0c34dd89187eef2a82e7df5abfabd2356205a8e68bf76b73e7c0193","tags":["deploy","security","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/smoke-remote.mjs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:30:25.931134Z","id":"76213ba062bf2f51a9dcb6b14732a6b6df46d9fd2be975b05fdd14f2720faa03","body":{"detail":"wrangler's docs say remote: true on an artifacts binding uses the remote service in local dev; whether that holds with --local and wrangler 4.149.0 is unverified. Locally the binding answers 'Binding ARTIFACTS needs to be run remotely'. If it works it gives a probe of the real service without a deploy.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":585},"end":{"line":590},"content_hash":"765d646f83c57f6bfd8c11ce9c56e0694989cbb0bd8310228dc0a9cf9e38cdfc"},"summary":"--remote-artifacts (the local Worker on the account's real Artifacts through the binding's remote: true) has not run: it needs a login, and harness.mjs starts wrangler dev with --local","supersedes":"4854d787a4833aea89d19dd5e75c7a3143dfe78c2612be02169652b1731c3277","tags":["deploy","artifacts","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/deploy.mjs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:47:22.853436Z","id":"68b4866befebe81db5fb79f0449259300706b9edbb38a54894bab2a3f596f838","body":{"detail":"The owner is told to delete the record once set up; CLAX_TOKEN there stays valid until rotated (deploy.mjs --rotate-secrets). An alternative is printing them only and having smoke-remote.mjs take them from the environment, at the cost of the one-command smoke.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":314},"end":{"line":319},"content_hash":"414d576933fd9210f222e847e6f372f2975ebe1fa1583e8a77b8eedd6675d13d"},"summary":"deploy.mjs keeps the generated SETUP_SECRET and CLAX_TOKEN in plain text in crates/clax-worker/.deploy/<public host>.json (0600, git-ignored) so smoke-remote.mjs can use them","supersedes":"bef595b64d34d5bcbde5cd7bd6be41ded484d86fee253b6418123a0514d03583","tags":["deploy","security","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/Cargo.lock","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T03:18:40.364921Z","id":"282372641c9aaf8a5802d2848adfba69d307843d292176dd78019231a61a29ff","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-worker is its own Cargo workspace with its own lockfile (crates/clax-worker/Cargo.toml), and 20e1ed98c3fc added roxmltree 0.20 to crates/clax-core/Cargo.toml and the root Cargo.lock only: the Worker lock's clax-core entry lists no roxmltree and the file has no roxmltree package. A --locked build of the Worker fails, and a build without it (worker-build, crates/clax-worker/build.sh) rewrites the lock, leaving a dirty tree. 2894d3f96 fixed the same kind of drift for dirs. roxmltree 0.20 itself suits wasm32: no dependencies, #![no_std] with an std feature, #![forbid(unsafe_code)], MIT OR Apache-2.0.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":279},"end":{"line":308},"content_hash":"302203f4a7f954b6abf500cbf5502f78b50dbc66192ffdec0786279f91bdda3b"},"suggested_fix":"Add roxmltree 0.20.0 to crates/clax-worker/Cargo.lock (its checksum is in the root Cargo.lock) and to clax-core's dependency list there.","summary":"The Worker's own Cargo.lock was not updated for clax-core's new roxmltree dependency","tags":["review","icon","wasm","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/Cargo.lock","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T05:35:11.460931Z","id":"4b2b5013b3ec188653a69446c5a24a583e211d66465702b05a11fdf95fe15662","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:20e1ed98c3fc","summary":"roxmltree 0.20.0 is locked and listed under clax-core. cargo metadata --locked --offline --manifest-path crates/clax-worker/Cargo.toml exited 101 ('cannot update the lock file ... because --locked was passed') before and 0 after; no target/ was made. No script in the repository checks the Worker lock's completeness (scripts/check-version.sh checks only Clax crates' versions).","supersedes":"282372641c9aaf8a5802d2848adfba69d307843d292176dd78019231a61a29ff","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/BUILD.bazel","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T20:43:54.351330Z","id":"348cfd981b134f9ae9e35fd3aa6991c70c25b7642b9d29ea094f8baaabee2db9","body":{"detail":"Only //crates/clax-worker:rustfmt is Bazel's; scripts/worker-checks.sh runs the Worker's tests and clippy with Cargo in CI's worker job. crates/clax-worker/Cargo.lock resolves the Clax crates' dependencies apart from the root's (on 2026-10-20 35 shared crates differ, e.g. tokio 1.53.2 vs 1.53.1, serde_json 1.0.154 vs 1.0.151, and 9 crates such as worker, worker-sys and strum are in it alone), so the Worker cannot link the root's //crates/* libraries built from @crates. A second crate_universe repo from the Worker's lockfile does not cover the Clax crates it uses by path: cargo-bazel copies such a path crate into an external repository (local_crate_mirror), where include_str! of files outside the crate (clax-core's ../../../web/extension/manifest.json, clax-server's web/contract/*.d.ts, clax-testkit's ../../clax-server/src/router.rs) does not resolve, and its hub aliases only the workspace members' direct dependencies, so first-party copies of those crates cannot name their third-party dependencies. Either way the Clax crates would be compiled a second time against other dependency versions, growing CI's 6 GB disk cache.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":1},"end":{"line":35},"content_hash":"a358426273ce7f971a79807f72458ef04df84e1eb64cf4174cee11cb52160f7c"},"summary":"Build and test crates/clax-worker and its VFS under Bazel (cargo_package, clippy aspect, rust_test), not only its format check","tags":["build","ci","revisit:crates/clax-worker joins the root Cargo workspace or shares its Cargo.lock, or rules_rust's crate_universe resolves path dependencies outside the workspace with their compile data","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/deploy.mjs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T14:16:42.606475Z","id":"5bf498465e85873b5d699d64bda22809932fa5719017cc0f82254d7fa4385a45","body":{"detail":"checkSiteHost counts any answer below 500 as the zone, the proxied * record, the certificate and the route *.<site>/* at work, assuming Cloudflare answers an unrouted proxied host with 52x or 530 and that the Worker (crates/clax-worker/src/lib.rs, once it serves site hosts) answers /_clax/healthz on a host naming no artifact with a status below 500. zoneFound, wildcardFound and certificateFound ran only against public hosts (cloudflare.com NS, www.cloudflare.com's addresses and certificate, a domain that does not resolve); the manual-step printout has not been seen on a deploy whose wildcard record or certificate is missing. The first deploy with --site-domain shows both.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":498},"end":{"line":518},"content_hash":"ce5f9b75d7d1cbbf3e7b5769fafdb0c50a3d655e068ad83e84ea50803c5fa91c"},"summary":"The site host check after a deploy has not run against a real Cloudflare account: what a Worker and the edge answer a random <ID>.<site domain>/_clax/healthz is assumed","tags":["deploy","unverified","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/smoke-remote.mjs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T14:16:42.606562Z","id":"3f70c4ddb76faba5f87d5af5edd2b05ee9c18a3703db2698d96b531e8a733212","body":{"detail":"The steps from 'site host: health' to 'site: two db artifacts kept apart' assume the routes and shapes the site-origins plan (docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-22-clax-run-site-origins.md, Tasks 3, 7, 8 and 11) gives: GET /site-signin 302 to <site>/_clax/session?code=, a site cookie named (__Host-)clax_site, POST /api/artifacts/<ID>/site-code answering {src}, a signed-out /_clax/api/whoami answering 401, PATCH /api/artifacts/<ID> taking site_access, and /_clax/api/docs/<path> answering {doc: {data}}. Until the Worker serves site hosts the health step skips on 404 and the rest skip with it. node --check passes; node smoke-remote.mjs --local has not run against a Worker with SITE_DOMAIN=localhost.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":420},"end":{"line":528},"content_hash":"b31026dff5bce5640009a0c441e68e628199c997eb52c67dce7696bf0b1af3b6"},"summary":"The smoke's site steps have not run: they need a Worker serving site hosts, and --local needs the wasm build","tags":["smoke","unverified","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/smoke-remote.mjs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T14:25:43.185779Z","id":"3aea74eefc0427252a3376bd12ec7e86c90256db44e9a2ec5083cea28ac4978c","body":{"kind":"comment","ref":"git:ef660002","references":"3f70c4ddb76faba5f87d5af5edd2b05ee9c18a3703db2698d96b531e8a733212","summary":"The health step now skips on 403 forbidden_host as well as 404: the Worker before site hosts refuses an unknown host with 403 {error:{code:\"forbidden_host\"}} (crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs:1486-1495), so the site steps skip there instead of failing. The world-open step checks the site_access PATCH's status and expects the signed-out navigation after closing to be a 302 to /site-signin. Still not run against a Worker serving site hosts.","tags":["session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/deploy.mjs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T14:25:43.185972Z","id":"88418f7f828ae8203b8898b1acb52b30c7114cb1903452b048816ab39167e4a6","body":{"kind":"comment","ref":"git:ef660002","references":"5bf498465e85873b5d699d64bda22809932fa5719017cc0f82254d7fa4385a45","summary":"The check no longer counts any answer below 500: siteHealthy (crates/clax-worker/deploy.mjs) requires the contract that /_clax/healthz on any well-formed site host, a random ID's included, answers 200 with /healthz's JSON (a version field) and Referrer-Policy: no-referrer. forbidden_host, Cloudflare's error pages, redirects and parking pages fail with the manual steps; test-deploy-config.mjs checks each shape against siteHealthy. The edge's real answers on a deploy are still unseen.","tags":["session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/deploy.mjs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T14:25:43.186031Z","id":"e64cd99b954bafe38c69f32ad5a7bf3f97cbb6b6fb6bc72eadcfe0f2d1d78d93","body":{"detail":"deployConfig writes SITE_DOMAIN and removes CONTENT_ORIGIN from wrangler.jsonc's vars, while crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs (var(env, \"CONTENT_ORIGIN\") near line 362) still reads only CONTENT_ORIGIN. Deployed together, the Worker would serve artifacts on no host. main() refuses a deploy that is neither --dry-run nor --config-only while workerReadsSiteDomain() finds no SITE_DOMAIN in src/instance.rs (test-deploy-config.mjs checks the refusal). The Worker change that reads SITE_DOMAIN (the site-origins plan's Task 11, docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-22-clax-run-site-origins.md) must land before this branch deploys; the guard is a substring check and turns off as soon as src/instance.rs names SITE_DOMAIN anywhere.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":360},"end":{"line":367},"content_hash":"396ee6580504102062f5b073e0aad024d8a9d29d1200ecc35767bb869c782540"},"summary":"The generated config drops CONTENT_ORIGIN and sets SITE_DOMAIN before the Worker reads SITE_DOMAIN; a real deploy is refused until crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs does","tags":["deploy","ordering","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/deploy.mjs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T14:28:30.455918Z","id":"7b1871184191296e02e3b4dd702066d2f1a53668fe2792f13d683a42f5544713","body":{"kind":"comment","ref":"git:fa26d5bf","references":"e64cd99b954bafe38c69f32ad5a7bf3f97cbb6b6fb6bc72eadcfe0f2d1d78d93","summary":"The guard is no longer a substring check: workerReadsSiteDomain matches the read var(env, \"SITE_DOMAIN\") in src/instance.rs, so a comment naming SITE_DOMAIN does not let a deploy through; test-deploy-config.mjs ('the guard matches the Worker's read of SITE_DOMAIN, not a mention') checks a read, a spaced read, a comment and the CONTENT_ORIGIN read.","tags":["session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/e2e-hosted.mjs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T16:15:08.354738Z","id":"ba616ada30c6f2ba75727d39aa714880661784740dade68f9044519efef78704","body":{"detail":"They follow the plan's interfaces for Tasks 3, 4 and 8 (302 to /site-signin, 401 site_session_required, PATCH site_access, a keyed /_blob/ URL serving no bytes); the first run after those land may need their expectations adjusted. The world-open steps also skip while PATCH site_access is refused.","kind":"concern","summary":"The site handshake, world-open and old keyed URL steps have only been written, not run: they skip while /site-signin answers 404 to the signed-in owner","tags":["deferred-work","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/e2e-hosted.mjs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T16:29:40.650258Z","id":"2e7d2d27e3baff9beadab8f3e2a61ba1ad183a08b42e8f42016e583c432bb735","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"ba616ada30c6f2ba75727d39aa714880661784740dade68f9044519efef78704","summary":"Since b744796e the steps skip only while the build has no access check at all: /site-signin answers 404 to the signed-in owner AND the private site is still served signed out (200). A site that refuses a signed-out caller (302 or 401) while /site-signin answers 404 fails the check 'a site that refuses signed-out callers has /site-signin to sign them in' (crates/clax-worker/e2e-hosted.mjs).","tags":["session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/deploy.mjs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T15:55:54.559159Z","id":"ea860275c783fb3c9d507fb6188bf8d1b662ce40ed86ee2068027ce5d0eab058","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:6d1e8cc8","summary":"Obsolete: crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs reads SITE_DOMAIN (site_hosts, var(env, \"SITE_DOMAIN\")), so the guard could no longer refuse a deploy; 6d1e8cc8 removes workerReadsSiteDomain, its call in main() and its test. Evidence: node test-deploy-config.mjs (in just worker-test) prints 'deploy config: all ok' with 16 checks.","supersedes":"e64cd99b954bafe38c69f32ad5a7bf3f97cbb6b6fb6bc72eadcfe0f2d1d78d93","tags":["reason:obsolete","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/e2e-hosted.mjs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T15:55:54.583019Z","id":"e22a4878191752512b6033b61183e25dfbeb8a86f2483b5829d98ca578433f33","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:abf0ab04","summary":"Fixed in abf0ab04: the site handshake, signed-out refusal and world-open steps are checks, no longer skipped, and they ran. Evidence: node e2e-hosted.mjs --no-build exits 0 with 88 ok lines, among them '/site-signin is served on the public origin', 'a private site signed out is sent to /site-signin on the public origin', 'a private site's subresource signed out is 401', 'the owner's browser opens the private site through the handshake' and 'PATCH site_access opens a site to the world'.","supersedes":"ba616ada30c6f2ba75727d39aa714880661784740dade68f9044519efef78704","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/Cargo.lock","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T10:42:13.941778Z","id":"2bb376a7369c5ce5d10c333cb9484621619aa68c70bec5d913e20bf60fed719e","body":{"detail":"clax-server depends on qrcode 0.14 (crates/clax-server/Cargo.toml, Cargo.toml workspace dependencies), and the workspace Cargo.lock has it, but the Worker's own lockfile was not updated. Running just worker-test adds qrcode 0.14.1 to the clax-server dependencies and a [[package]] entry, leaving the checkout dirty.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":436},"end":{"line":470},"content_hash":"18ba4a79ad2d879595f2009ec192db670f0e156e278b0c723ed417e9db0fbe74"},"suggested_fix":"Run the Worker's build once (just worker-test) and commit the updated crates/clax-worker/Cargo.lock.","summary":"crates/clax-worker/Cargo.lock does not list qrcode, so the next Worker build rewrites it","tags":["app-push","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/Cargo.lock","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T10:46:50.293448Z","id":"7b5b3c49665d8ef920f65d7a5fcbe5d3397e090642e5aa99995a772b650dc855","body":{"detail":"clax-server depends on qrcode 0.14 (crates/clax-server/Cargo.toml, Cargo.toml workspace dependencies), and the workspace Cargo.lock has it, but the Worker's own lockfile was not updated. Running just worker-test adds qrcode 0.14.1 to the clax-server dependencies and a [[package]] entry, leaving the checkout dirty.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":436},"end":{"line":469},"content_hash":"7ec6d4b3ab978bb73d23396d8a9e3c1ee77f2aa3a8bcbfd0d83f54a6760d5ee0"},"suggested_fix":"Run the Worker's build once (just worker-test) and commit the updated crates/clax-worker/Cargo.lock.","summary":"crates/clax-worker/Cargo.lock does not list qrcode, so the next Worker build rewrites it","supersedes":"2bb376a7369c5ce5d10c333cb9484621619aa68c70bec5d913e20bf60fed719e","tags":["app-push","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/Cargo.lock","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T11:42:19.044681Z","id":"143b8d1737a05a3d5c6add4ed60ddc83c33cd4f72502964e529c3a610129b22d","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:e3dc56eff","summary":"crates/clax-worker/Cargo.lock now lists qrcode 0.14.1 under clax-server. just worker-test exited 0 (cargo test, clippy and test-wasm.mjs all ok) and left git status clean after the commit.","supersedes":"7b5b3c49665d8ef920f65d7a5fcbe5d3397e090642e5aa99995a772b650dc855","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/test-bot.mjs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T12:17:22.421002Z","id":"8af08fe94af92dbc3abda2cb5071068933c7981737264693959eb1560aca0df9","body":{"detail":"ServerHost::write, publish and reply return not_yet (crates/clax-server/src/bot.rs). The script catches the error and the test prints a note; once the host writes, the same check asserts version 2 and a reply comment.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":323},"end":{"line":325},"content_hash":"3b64a2fb750d997b493bf64ffdb09bc7ebef7d1a9a87bf5c28d240894f99e4e5"},"summary":"test-bot.mjs checks the script's publish and reply only once clax_server::bot::ServerHost writes: it answers unavailable now, so a run's publish and thread reply have not run on the Worker","tags":["hosted","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/deploy.mjs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T12:17:22.421638Z","id":"28d3ddb69b2ab8505360c7ea4882038615cec8a50c3bd3ca061def2131386dc2","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"68b4866befebe81db5fb79f0449259300706b9edbb38a54894bab2a3f596f838","summary":"The record now also keeps CLAX_KEK (kek), ClaxBot's key-encryption key, in the same 0600 file: it is the only copy outside the Worker's secrets, and losing both loses every stored model key. deploy.mjs re-uploads the record's kek to a Worker that has none (kekPlan) and never rotates it.","tags":["hosted","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/deploy.mjs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T12:18:19.734121Z","id":"ef20c1430e47689279bf7bc60d52dc32cc806bfd62a89382b7fecb01b16060cf","body":{"detail":"Only the logged-out --dry-run ran (no account was available): node deploy.mjs --dry-run --zone example.com passes and ends at wrangler deploy --dry-run (11.36 MiB, 4.36 MiB gzipped). Each logged-in step throws with wrangler's last error line and the command it ran, so a wrong pattern shows as a failed step rather than silently. If namespaces list answers a shape jsonIn does not parse, the namespace is taken as missing and a probe repository is created and deleted, which is harmless.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":168},"end":{"line":238},"content_hash":"b56127513f46b546e759ff598045a8c339be77ca93970ddebc103f6ecf534fe1"},"summary":"deploy.mjs's logged-in paths have not run: the whoami --json accounts shape, the 'already exists' patterns for r2 bucket create and queues create, artifacts namespaces list --json's shape, secret list --format json, and the account-scoped deploy with --secrets-file","supersedes":"61c8252ad530041c277dd059809fb9481703393efcc1eced47a4d98523f42ed2","tags":["deploy","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/deploy.mjs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T12:18:19.757541Z","id":"47c3324f0ca30c3624c5a4c17f6eb597d51aeceaf9c7001b01f95e3f558cfb8a","body":{"detail":"The owner is told to delete the record once set up; CLAX_TOKEN there stays valid until rotated (deploy.mjs --rotate-secrets). An alternative is printing them only and having smoke-remote.mjs take them from the environment, at the cost of the one-command smoke.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":359},"end":{"line":363},"content_hash":"3f792a4841158150d836d343a2870bf4d63b9230c6b3a056b523f45beb8e9736"},"summary":"deploy.mjs keeps the generated SETUP_SECRET and CLAX_TOKEN in plain text in crates/clax-worker/.deploy/<public host>.json (0600, git-ignored) so smoke-remote.mjs can use them","supersedes":"68b4866befebe81db5fb79f0449259300706b9edbb38a54894bab2a3f596f838","tags":["deploy","security","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/deploy.mjs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T14:15:16.321482Z","id":"6c3a6172414d9f9f5c2de1eff485fbc596bf1b650d0f0841091a29ba1434b285","body":{"detail":"The owner is told to delete the record once set up; CLAX_TOKEN there stays valid until rotated (deploy.mjs --rotate-secrets). An alternative is printing them only and having smoke-remote.mjs take them from the environment, at the cost of the one-command smoke.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":394},"end":{"line":398},"content_hash":"3f792a4841158150d836d343a2870bf4d63b9230c6b3a056b523f45beb8e9736"},"summary":"deploy.mjs keeps the generated SETUP_SECRET and CLAX_TOKEN in plain text in crates/clax-worker/.deploy/<public host>.json (0600, git-ignored) so smoke-remote.mjs can use them","supersedes":"47c3324f0ca30c3624c5a4c17f6eb597d51aeceaf9c7001b01f95e3f558cfb8a","tags":["deploy","security","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/test-bot.mjs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T14:15:16.455516Z","id":"a248e2712f29c0cd33c13166341305b5ed4b9cbcb5bfb84e6acc6b22e9a30460","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:88645653","summary":"Fixed: ServerHost writes, and test-bot.mjs asserts the script publishes version 2 and replies once on the Worker, once each across the restart (node test-bot.mjs --no-build: 41 checks ok, three runs)","supersedes":"8af08fe94af92dbc3abda2cb5071068933c7981737264693959eb1560aca0df9","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/deploy.mjs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T14:57:57.599175Z","id":"b5337d60198aaedf61e6c4884c50d897729ef7e27b3ee45d65aef2d0f8715a05","body":{"detail":"The owner is told to delete the record once set up; CLAX_TOKEN there stays valid until rotated (deploy.mjs --rotate-secrets). An alternative is printing them only and having smoke-remote.mjs take them from the environment, at the cost of the one-command smoke.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":401},"end":{"line":405},"content_hash":"3f792a4841158150d836d343a2870bf4d63b9230c6b3a056b523f45beb8e9736"},"summary":"deploy.mjs keeps the generated SETUP_SECRET and CLAX_TOKEN in plain text in crates/clax-worker/.deploy/<public host>.json (0600, git-ignored) so smoke-remote.mjs can use them","supersedes":"6c3a6172414d9f9f5c2de1eff485fbc596bf1b650d0f0841091a29ba1434b285","tags":["deploy","security","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/deploy.mjs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T14:57:57.864038Z","id":"79115d20b0d6d78bb0b08bc5777657eb5448ab91a58eaed51a906fd7e81ffeb0","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"b5337d60198aaedf61e6c4884c50d897729ef7e27b3ee45d65aef2d0f8715a05","summary":"Since 59aca7bd and 904a6c2a CLAX_KEK is no longer kept in this record: deploy.mjs writes it to its own file, <host>.kek beside the record (0600), before the deploy, and moves a kek an old record held there; the record can be deleted once set up without losing the key.","tags":["session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/Cargo.toml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T15:50:56.264687Z","id":"4d7886934936f4b856641f9d67fd21578b7e0e09fc66ff1245d28a61fe033956","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-worker is its own workspace and uses clax-core, clax-rt and clax-server by path; its Cargo.lock was extended from the spike's, not seeded from the root Cargo.lock. A dependency the root pins (axum 0.8.9, rusqlite 0.40.2 agree today) can drift. Joining the root workspace would share one lockfile but pull workers-rs into every native build.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":25},"end":{"line":35},"content_hash":"c16d1c5374aac148adc8a5c3a92f7090bef7dea4c8289b36e3c487a974f7d454"},"summary":"The Worker's lockfile resolves the Clax crates' dependencies apart from the root's, so the Worker may build them at other versions than the daemon","supersedes":"af73cb2ed383f881021b778eb2194604afc102070e02a2aec2299aed7bb0c6b6","tags":["session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/smoke-remote.mjs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T21:39:11.717069Z","id":"821dc738e2b2406e5706c499d1b067e7bca9ca4fa323a3765e2b65520b4807de","body":{"detail":"wrangler's docs say remote: true on an artifacts binding uses the remote service in local dev; whether that holds with --local and wrangler 4.149.0 is unverified. Locally the binding answers 'Binding ARTIFACTS needs to be run remotely'. If it works it gives a probe of the real service without a deploy.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":585},"end":{"line":590},"content_hash":"c0935c9bbbe35e49293dcac7515e8ce205120fcb62409d2fb0736bea75443e12"},"summary":"--remote-artifacts (the local Worker on the account's real Artifacts through the binding's remote: true) has not run: it needs a login, and harness.mjs starts wrangler dev with --local","supersedes":"76213ba062bf2f51a9dcb6b14732a6b6df46d9fd2be975b05fdd14f2720faa03","tags":["deploy","artifacts","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/deploy.mjs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T21:39:12.372012Z","id":"6030d730445d226f6933d8f213d639301adb7d21863e9fc5d446b9c1e94b82d0","body":{"detail":"Only the logged-out --dry-run ran (no account was available): node deploy.mjs --dry-run --zone example.com passes and ends at wrangler deploy --dry-run (11.36 MiB, 4.36 MiB gzipped). Each logged-in step throws with wrangler's last error line and the command it ran, so a wrong pattern shows as a failed step rather than silently. If namespaces list answers a shape jsonIn does not parse, the namespace is taken as missing and a probe repository is created and deleted, which is harmless.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":171},"end":{"line":241},"content_hash":"27c3df423ef169242ce5f7773385ef1089a3e1ce7a54a59824526a08bc5654ef"},"summary":"deploy.mjs's logged-in paths have not run: the whoami --json accounts shape, the 'already exists' patterns for r2 bucket create and queues create, artifacts namespaces list --json's shape, secret list --format json, and the account-scoped deploy with --secrets-file","supersedes":"ef20c1430e47689279bf7bc60d52dc32cc806bfd62a89382b7fecb01b16060cf","tags":["deploy","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/deploy.mjs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T21:39:13.058504Z","id":"78c3d28f66447e45d9bb25efa26a44ec0047d42496516bc2cc11485046c3dcd0","body":{"detail":"The owner is told to delete the record once set up; CLAX_TOKEN there stays valid until rotated (deploy.mjs --rotate-secrets). An alternative is printing them only and having smoke-remote.mjs take them from the environment, at the cost of the one-command smoke.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":461},"end":{"line":465},"content_hash":"04f426f78fc1161fc839ffdeaf491f98a731bf681600b862f78fc7d078df8237"},"summary":"deploy.mjs keeps the generated SETUP_SECRET and CLAX_TOKEN in plain text in crates/clax-worker/.deploy/<public host>.json (0600, git-ignored) so smoke-remote.mjs can use them","supersedes":"b5337d60198aaedf61e6c4884c50d897729ef7e27b3ee45d65aef2d0f8715a05","tags":["deploy","security","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/smoke-remote.mjs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T17:06:35.382925Z","id":"5a5d333772b5f07e87afa568f2bf65efe627fdb02ab52a74272b14b11c11baa3","body":{"detail":"When setup is closed and no --session is given, the owner step (OWNER) sets c.as = \"token\": the 'agent token' step skips, because POST /api/hosted/agent-tokens is browser_only (crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs mint_token refuses any request with Authorization), and the MCP steps run as the daemon token's sessionless agent (no Mcp-Session-Id). The agent-token path (minting, the cxa_ bearer on /mcp, its per-initialize session, revocation) is then covered only by the first deploy's smoke, by --session, and by e2e-hosted.mjs on a local Worker. Options: keep the skip (today's behaviour); or add a narrow owner-token route that mints and revokes an agent token for the owner, with tests and contract text, so every release smoke covers it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":286},"end":{"line":291},"content_hash":"a7ad150b792fea0e1d05a24eca45ee15f11a8490f657cd5454870de1f80f6f19"},"summary":"On every deploy after the first the smoke acts with the owner token, so it never mints an agent token or opens an agent token's MCP session","tags":["deploy","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/deploy.mjs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T17:06:35.383014Z","id":"c190906e5b7f2a3eaa221fd54bc5f460361479b68b016344e57bb4de464637e8","body":{"detail":"partialTriggerUpdate (crates/clax-worker/deploy-lib.mjs) is tested on fixture strings built around the line wrangler printed, 'Trigger configuration for \"clax\" was only partially updated' (Cloudflare API code 10013 on the custom-domains call); the rest of that output was not captured, so a wording change in wrangler would make the deploy fail as before rather than retry. waitHealthy now waits until /healthz reports the CLAX_BUILD var of this upload; the local Worker reports it (node smoke-remote.mjs --local shows build smoke-local-<run> and the commit), but no real custom domain has answered with it yet.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":547},"end":{"line":561},"content_hash":"c52f4f4af4aabc9f0f21d053bcad373055a7b16159834bdc23daa5cf2deb482d"},"summary":"The partial-trigger retry and the build-matching health wait have not run against the real account","tags":["deploy","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/deploy.mjs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T17:06:35.383053Z","id":"a2d881e80dc714c22efd5ee9efa931d9187bb3a73f27ff3b6fe1efea92dbf470","body":{"detail":"buildId takes sourceCommit() (git rev-parse HEAD) at deploy time, but --no-build uploads build/index_bg.wasm from an earlier build. The ID stays unique per upload, so the health wait is right; the /healthz commit field (CLAX_BUILD_COMMIT stamped at build time, src/instance.rs BUILD_COMMIT) is the one that names the binary's commit.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":455},"end":{"line":456},"content_hash":"dc9d43ddf3868cb2aa523db60d83ae38ef16a1bd1f7d011ef6c2def689a6e31c"},"summary":"With --no-build the build ID's commit prefix is the checked-out HEAD, which may not be the commit the uploaded Worker was built from","tags":["deploy","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/deploy.mjs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T18:19:38.524822Z","id":"159f8a6219d1612a897c13c8b6fb2d25c373e8823e0e6f7f2c000a5cb0172343","body":{"detail":"login() reads `wrangler whoami --json`'s loggedIn and accounts; under an API token (the deploy workflow's credential, scripts/cloudflare-setup.sh --ci) neither field's shape has been seen, and an account list the token may not read falls back to --account as `(given)`. secretNames (deploy.mjs) answers [] when `wrangler secret list` fails, so a token lacking the permission reads as a Worker without secrets: --ci then refuses as for a first deploy (ciSecretsRefusal names both causes), which is safe but sends the reader to the wrong cause. Verified only: `node deploy.mjs --ci --dry-run --no-build …` without a login, and `node deploy.mjs --ci …` refusing with 'not logged in: --ci signs in with CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN'.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":347},"end":{"line":366},"content_hash":"2a5d5de88a865d1bba3fdb63f6a9d55f0896d4c4d6590919017899c1e3603e57"},"summary":"deploy.mjs --ci has not run against Cloudflare: login() with CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN in place of `wrangler login` is assumed","tags":["untested","deploy","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/deploy.mjs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T18:19:38.525059Z","id":"20d2b5f1d1df84f07cb27bbd635d91d14b717bc259fb09357ea963f64caae958","body":{"detail":"A laptop deploy reads the retired content origin from its record; a --ci deploy keeps its record in a fresh $CLAX_DEPLOY_HOME, so the flag is its only source. checkCiOptions (crates/clax-worker/deploy-lib.mjs) cannot require it, since most instances have none, and nothing on the account is read to tell. The deploy workflow's environment must carry it for an instance that has one. The GitHub sign-in has a guard of this kind (ciSecretsRefusal refuses when the Worker has GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET but no --github-client-id was given); the retired host has none.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":723},"end":{"line":723},"content_hash":"df89f6875e869fbbd27c8c852cc5a3c5d7f28cd379c0afd92a65b6e13da82944"},"summary":"A --ci deploy that is not given --retired-content-origin drops the retired content host's route and RETIRED_CONTENT_ORIGIN without noticing","tags":["deploy","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/deploy.mjs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T18:19:38.525186Z","id":"5011f7746278cfcb716e869f3ca10c18f7da24099ece534b65ca8812981247bb","body":{"detail":"checkProduction runs again just before `wrangler deploy`, so only prod's tip at upload time reaches production. When prod moves during a deploy's build, that run fails (GitHub notifies the owner) and the deploy queued for the newer push deploys the new tip. Accepted: a red run for a superseded commit over an upload of a commit that is no longer prod's tip.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":861},"end":{"line":861},"content_hash":"34a9eed2ca450770f4a47a92a272338f62041a60fce6eb95e7793da224e49836"},"summary":"A production deploy whose prod tip moved while it built fails before the upload, failing its run","tags":["deploy","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/smoke-remote.mjs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T18:19:38.530721Z","id":"670802195d6e8203bf33c91a9897c66b4c6b6ba8445ea66dccd1bbe7850bfcba","body":{"detail":"As an agent token (CLAX_SMOKE_TOKEN) the smoke has no diagnostics, so on REPO_STORE=artifacts the push becomes a version only through the queue's pushed event for the subscription this step makes with `wrangler queues subscription create`; the direct-reconcile fallback needs the owner token. A token without Queues edit fails this step, and 'the push becomes a version' then fails after --queue-wait. Not run: --local --as-agent uses REPO_STORE=memory, where the step skips.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":753},"end":{"line":769},"content_hash":"e28d4154f94ceba956bb0bb6725d5c02b0724ff5eaf130ab8fbbd586232826f9"},"summary":"The queue subscription step runs with the deploy workflow's CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN, whose Queues permission is not known; without it the push steps fail the deploy","tags":["untested","deploy","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/deploy-lib.mjs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T18:19:38.530813Z","id":"fe517211db8ae7da4a26bd3306d97272e36b39d22b8882e645b234486796ede6","body":{"detail":"`node smoke-remote.mjs --local --no-build --as-agent` without these skips answered: the shell's pages 403 forbidden ('agents of another machine may not use this route'), POST /api/artifacts/<ID>/site-code 403, PATCH /api/artifacts/<ID> and POST /api/artifacts/<ID>/fork 400 no_session, and /api/stream's WebSocket closed 1006; with them, 15 ok, 0 failed, 11 skipped. That opening a site to the world waits on its person's approval is read from crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs set_site_access (approval_pending), not run. None of it has run against a deployed Worker.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":185},"end":{"line":207},"content_hash":"d2b2862715915f7dfd975cd816ee4dbe4193a098a62b4ebfcfbd263c421c3a1c"},"summary":"SMOKE_CANNOT.agent's reasons were seen only under wrangler dev --local, and opening a site to the world only in the MCP tool's code","tags":["untested","smoke","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/smoke-remote.mjs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T18:19:38.531950Z","id":"6a5d1611b874ed3f7b24c0cb1e5349bf95fcb7c11345ebf78dcdd880b4d55677","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"5a5d333772b5f07e87afa568f2bf65efe627fdb02ab52a74272b14b11c11baa3","summary":"With CLAX_SMOKE_TOKEN (or --agent-token) the smoke now acts as an agent token and opens its MCP session on any deploy, as the deploy workflow runs it; `node smoke-remote.mjs --local --no-build --as-agent` passes (15 ok, 0 failed, 11 skipped). The owner-token path described here still mints none.","tags":["session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/deploy.mjs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T20:08:52.711104Z","id":"79cb1669c06a6f23f35275a94793f0f6454772ff96fd64feab7ef7b26f662b66","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:3d0e9dcd5","summary":"Fixed: with --no-build, deploy.mjs now refuses a build/index_bg.wasm that does not embed the checked-out HEAD (deploy-lib.mjs builtFromRefusal; the Worker embeds CLAX_BUILD_COMMIT, src/instance.rs BUILD_COMMIT), so the build ID's commit prefix names the uploaded Worker's commit. Evidence: node --test crates/clax-worker/deploy-lib.test.mjs passes, and its '--no-build deploys only a Worker built from the checked-out commit' test fails when the commit check is removed.","supersedes":"a2d881e80dc714c22efd5ee9efa931d9187bb3a73f27ff3b6fe1efea92dbf470","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/deploy.mjs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T20:08:52.815750Z","id":"6d6fd91607e54b7ba90a7ba2fa867af6f45b51edbaf26cf182ed5eaf220fbba8","body":{"detail":"It assumes build/index_bg.wasm holds CLAX_BUILD_COMMIT's 40 hex characters as one run of bytes (src/instance.rs BUILD_COMMIT, an option_env! &str passed to clax_core::set_build_commit). deploy-lib.test.mjs checks the function on made-up bytes only. If a release build stored the string otherwise, every --no-build deploy, the Deploy prod workflow's included, would fail with 'was not built from HEAD'. Check: CLAX_BUILD_COMMIT=$(git rev-parse HEAD) crates/clax-worker/build.sh, then grep -c $(git rev-parse HEAD) crates/clax-worker/build/index_bg.wasm.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":846},"end":{"line":852},"content_hash":"6136822cc725628cb0f90b4d227b64fd81396bbf0e023f294fb592b979689c12"},"summary":"builtFromRefusal's commit check has not run against a real Worker build","tags":["untested","deploy","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/deploy.mjs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T20:09:40.400656Z","id":"5549f4fd13a1e173e8142cd3f23e13b054f76005d3b6db7a7ace19a4b3d1eed3","body":{"kind":"resolve","summary":"Checked against a real release build: crates/clax-worker/build/index_bg.wasm from the deploy of f57ec462b (build f57ec462bb3b-20261026T144011Z) contains the full commit; `strings build/index_bg.wasm | grep -oE '[0-9a-f]{12,40}' | grep ^f57ec462` prints f57ec462bb3b3df5cf68be5b38ac4f6e7db29a8f.","supersedes":"6d6fd91607e54b7ba90a7ba2fa867af6f45b51edbaf26cf182ed5eaf220fbba8","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/build.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-28T20:06:09.908414Z","id":"1bfaeae7c4c1e6b81acc19ff3699d9691044b1449d07299de3827d6523e804a0","body":{"detail":"lane_worker in scripts/quality_gates.sh runs crates/clax-worker/test-wasm.mjs, which runs build.sh: off macOS it uses clang and the newest llvm-ar* on PATH, and on its first run cargo installs worker-build 0.8.7 into target/tools (minutes, cold). .github/workflows/ci.yml:13 and rust-toolchain.toml add the wasm32-unknown-unknown target. Whether ubuntu-latest's clang targets wasm32 and has an llvm-ar, and how long the lane takes cold there, was not checked; the first CI run shows it.\n\nRe-anchored unchanged from the record 7a96ebb5 (mailto:alex@kesling.co, session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347) onto the lines it concerns, which moved when crates/clax-worker joined the root workspace and Bazel's build.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":38},"end":{"line":44},"content_hash":"e44a55c588a089a34b64b90fa2e15f74fac1916c71913f6ebf4cd50f2e757a16"},"summary":"The worker lane's wasm build has run only on macOS: CI's Ubuntu runner and build.sh's Linux branch are unverified","supersedes":"7a96ebb5ba932b732f23b33736801444b64544c02261b89bafd8ba593ec05bae","tags":["gates","ci","session:claude-code:02ec6080-e7bb-4940-94c1-2f7bed23b002"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/e2e-publish.mjs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-28T20:06:10.014925Z","id":"4dbcddaf61eed8dddbd8c5981e859a5c59df8937c3e69b0f7320e79948543e57","body":{"detail":"Like e2e-hosted.mjs, it runs only by hand (npm run e2e:publish with CLAX_TEST_BIN set), since it needs a clax binary beside the Worker build. The native path is covered in the gates by crates/clax-server/tests/api_remotes.rs and crates/clax-cli/tests/remote_push.rs.\n\nRe-anchored unchanged from the record e7e61e07 (mailto:alex@kesling.co, session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347) onto the lines it concerns, which moved when crates/clax-worker joined the root workspace and Bazel's build.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1},"end":{"line":12},"content_hash":"42e3bd4cd360bb0a112a7e6b8b5b0fa70ef2613a78dca6c1b161d9210b2eb443"},"summary":"The Worker's publish e2e is not run by scripts/quality_gates.sh","supersedes":"e7e61e071d45155206aa092dc95df07d7f20eb8b84162af3b2867e2c9de80a56","tags":["testing","session:claude-code:02ec6080-e7bb-4940-94c1-2f7bed23b002"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/test-repos.mjs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-28T20:06:10.349891Z","id":"61a1882808f9f9ce84ea41b44fb28c84293443568a61acb26df6dc0e8a0fc15e","body":{"detail":"Run in sequence after the other Worker e2e lanes; two later runs alone passed. The Worker answers the oversized body before reading it (the body caps), which wrangler dev's proxy sometimes turns into a lost connection. The e2e-hosted lane follows its chunked oversized bodies with a request that may fail for the same reason.\n\nRe-anchored unchanged from the record a3e8251c (mailto:alex@kesling.co, session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347) onto the lines it concerns, which moved when crates/clax-worker joined the root workspace and Bazel's build.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":586},"end":{"line":587},"content_hash":"df0793a0b2b4eb9b97ad52f463593d700501072fbce6616032fdcc9bf4fc1e85"},"summary":"The 13 MiB push check failed once in three runs: git saw HTTP 500 where 413 was expected, wrangler logging 'Network connection lost' for the receive-pack POST","supersedes":"a3e8251c3f14d646150e8c2a8d326dd42aa53683c1de7647a870e7959b5737cc","tags":["worker","test","flake","session:claude-code:02ec6080-e7bb-4940-94c1-2f7bed23b002"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/BUILD.bazel","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-28T20:06:10.570075Z","id":"487c9d997227c7c95ea94ca38d9fbd6dfceb40c791e343f8aca6ef1aa6e61325","body":{"detail":"bazel build //crates/clax-worker:bundle took 962 s on an Apple silicon Mac with no wasm32 output cached (critical path 929 s: the wasm32 compiles of the Worker's crates, then the final link), under the worker-release profile (opt-level z, fat LTO, one codegen unit) over about 300 crates. Bazel caches it, but an edit to any workspace crate the Worker builds (clax-core, clax-server and the rest) relinks it, and CI's bazel job builds it in its full pass, as the wrangler and browser tests depend on it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":38},"end":{"line":46},"content_hash":"11b5aff78fccd15ed56f54d476c0bcb3884b2141f63b526193b7e08499b28ff4"},"suggested_fix":"Build the tests' bundle with thin LTO and more codegen units, and keep the worker-release settings for the deploy's build only.","summary":"A cold build of the Worker's bundle takes about 16 minutes, and any change to a crate the Worker builds relinks it","tags":["session:claude-code:02ec6080-e7bb-4940-94c1-2f7bed23b002"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/BUILD.bazel","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-28T20:06:37.922505Z","id":"70c0a781a59f776a452f907f6afb219da4be5ebf8f116fe967cae062941a0300","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"348cfd981b134f9ae9e35fd3aa6991c70c25b7642b9d29ea094f8baaabee2db9","summary":"Taken: crates/clax-worker joined the root workspace and its Cargo.lock (commit 4279e2c86), which this alternative's revisit tag names, so the Worker and its VFS are cargo_package() crates whose tests and clippy Bazel runs; its wasm32 build has its own crate universe, @crates_wasm (0cc15e9bb, bazel/wasm/README.md). Proposed close: obsolete.","tags":["session:claude-code:02ec6080-e7bb-4940-94c1-2f7bed23b002"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/build.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-28T20:06:37.923260Z","id":"4598759a4d9544ea7c0a676b081748962a7cd775c6dfdf3c7d3a2e0945e61e8e","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"1bfaeae7c4c1e6b81acc19ff3699d9691044b1449d07299de3827d6523e804a0","summary":"build.sh now builds with Bazel when it is installed (//crates/clax-worker:bundle), and CI's bazel job builds that, not this native branch. The Linux side of the Bazel build is unverified too: concern c853265a on bazel/wasm/README.md:43:62.","tags":["session:claude-code:02ec6080-e7bb-4940-94c1-2f7bed23b002"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/deploy.mjs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-28T20:06:37.923998Z","id":"74d7e724589c13e02e3e655b0b9c0a5920cf5ecedd13c085b7239e2e94418758","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"a2d881e80dc714c22efd5ee9efa931d9187bb3a73f27ff3b6fe1efea92dbf470","summary":"/healthz's commit now comes from the CLAX_BUILD_COMMIT var deploy.mjs writes from the checked-out HEAD (commit 7ac6caf74, src/instance.rs build_commit), so it shares this limitation: with --no-build it names HEAD whatever commit the bundle was built from.","tags":["session:claude-code:02ec6080-e7bb-4940-94c1-2f7bed23b002"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/Cargo.toml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-28T20:07:01.555453Z","id":"159b3b8e5a18c8baaae2bf6b5bc8e0adbef57805bdceacdaab64b86901d124bf","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:4279e2c86","summary":"crates/clax-worker and crates/clax-worker/vfs are members of the root workspace and crates/clax-worker/Cargo.lock is gone: `ls crates/clax-worker/Cargo.lock` reports No such file or directory, and `cargo metadata --locked` at the root lists clax-worker and clax-do-vfs as workspace members, so the Worker builds every Clax crate's dependencies at the root Cargo.lock's versions. Joining the workspace does not pull workers-rs into a plain native build: Cargo.toml's default-members leave the Worker out.","supersedes":"4d7886934936f4b856641f9d67fd21578b7e0e09fc66ff1245d28a61fe033956","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:02ec6080-e7bb-4940-94c1-2f7bed23b002"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/build.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T01:37:41.909891Z","id":"8972497c701838170ec56ef581c4bcf6dab2e63daeed2c0f9d18dee11d59c2a7","body":{"detail":"lane_worker in scripts/quality_gates.sh runs crates/clax-worker/test-wasm.mjs, which runs build.sh: off macOS it uses clang and the newest llvm-ar* on PATH, and on its first run cargo installs worker-build 0.8.7 into target/tools (minutes, cold). .github/workflows/ci.yml:13 and rust-toolchain.toml add the wasm32-unknown-unknown target. Whether ubuntu-latest's clang targets wasm32 and has an llvm-ar, and how long the lane takes cold there, was not checked; the first CI run shows it.\n\nRe-anchored unchanged from the record 7a96ebb5 (mailto:alex@kesling.co, session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347) onto the lines it concerns, which moved when crates/clax-worker joined the root workspace and Bazel's build.\n\nRe-anchored again onto the same lines, which moved when build.sh began recording its build (built-from.json).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":58},"end":{"line":64},"content_hash":"e44a55c588a089a34b64b90fa2e15f74fac1916c71913f6ebf4cd50f2e757a16"},"summary":"The worker lane's wasm build has run only on macOS: CI's Ubuntu runner and build.sh's Linux branch are unverified","supersedes":"1bfaeae7c4c1e6b81acc19ff3699d9691044b1449d07299de3827d6523e804a0","tags":["gates","ci","session:claude-code:02ec6080-e7bb-4940-94c1-2f7bed23b002"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/test-repos.mjs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T00:42:43.940402Z","id":"94f88b0a43f0170445d362504394e9df8507c3c9db564bbddf116275274e1726","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"a3e8251c3f14d646150e8c2a8d326dd42aa53683c1de7647a870e7959b5737cc","summary":"The same 500-for-413 shape in crates/clax-worker/e2e-hosted.mjs: CI run 40793343314's worker job failed 'a chunked body past 96 MiB is refused 413' (e2e-hosted.mjs:319) with 500, after the declared-length and 16 MiB chunked checks passed. The job passed on the two runs before it with no change under crates/clax-worker between them.","tags":["session:claude-code:52195316-c20b-49ba-9ad3-4026c7d5a1e0"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/build.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T01:56:56.817982Z","id":"80395d0ec8a6f1c12b6f42c9ed02d7e68d76852e92225489762735e300c734ba","body":{"detail":"cargo install worker-build@0.8.7 --locked builds from worker-build's published Cargo.lock, which pins the yanked yoke-derive 0.8.3 (cargo warns 'package yoke-derive v0.8.3 in Cargo.lock is yanked'; this crate's own Cargo.lock has 0.8.4), and cargo then warns to add target/tools/bin to PATH, which does not apply: line 23 runs worker-build by its full path. Dropping --locked clears the first at the cost of an unpinned tool build; --quiet hides both along with cargo's progress. Both go away when worker-build is no longer installed here (a Bazel-built Worker), or with a worker-build release whose lockfile has moved off the yanked version.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":10},"end":{"line":12},"content_hash":"cda61c6edd3a1479c1fcf7bec21b050719a5135f9f55a0aa1a08903158edd3a4"},"summary":"The one-time worker-build install prints two warnings no change in this repository can clear","tags":["build","worker","session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/build.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T02:54:59.762889Z","id":"d6a756b3e6f3b29e3f1c1f9bee647cb5e6cda54302739f0272e43b3f6ee6d35c","body":{"detail":"On the native path only (with Bazel, build.sh builds //crates/clax-worker:bundle and installs nothing). cargo install worker-build@0.8.7 --locked builds from worker-build's published Cargo.lock, which pins the yanked yoke-derive 0.8.3 (cargo warns 'package yoke-derive v0.8.3 in Cargo.lock is yanked'; the root Cargo.lock has its own yoke-derive), and cargo then warns to add target/tools/bin to PATH, which does not apply: build.sh runs worker-build by its full path. Dropping --locked clears the first at the cost of an unpinned tool build; --quiet hides both along with cargo's progress. Both go away with a worker-build release whose lockfile has moved off the yanked version.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":54},"end":{"line":57},"content_hash":"ea77eaa9102406c3f3ae1464ad8a7025d2eea7e4c2e1e910a0feb89459daf147"},"summary":"Without Bazel, the one-time worker-build install prints two warnings no change in this repository can clear","supersedes":"80395d0ec8a6f1c12b6f42c9ed02d7e68d76852e92225489762735e300c734ba","tags":["build","worker","session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
